<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7032"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:witchkingofangmar@comcast.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Witchking<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Witchking<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 9:05 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Okay, the guy is a cryptogram puzzle freak correct? He LOVES word puzzles even inventing them for police? <BR>Remember the movie Wargames? Would you like to play a game? &#40;I KNOW the movie wasn&#39;t until 1980 or so&#41; BUT nonetheless, from the moment this clown started with word puzzles let&#39;s take the initials of the victims &#40;and Anne Williams or her daughter and now MAYBE the ones north of town&#41; and see just what the initials might spell. Anyone wanting to jump in feel free but if he really want to leave clues, and loves word games, let&#39;s get going on this....<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7032-->
<!--Post: 7329--><!--Time: 1108404103-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7329"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rebtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rebtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 10:01 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I put the BTK cipher into monoalphabetic substitution program that I downloaded off the internet.   <BR> <BR>This what I put in.  <BR>vsnhlwibysoyvbueoedonewpsiodjncletoahlinoeteeievow dsalecntenoollieameo. <BR> <BR>This is the what I got after about 45min of trying to solve this. <BR>fgastohing1infiveledidaeoughidcapterlysthalereehef lodgytepareallttheywel. <BR> <BR>Maybe some of you crypotlogist&#39;s can make heads or tails of this. If this means anything to any one please let me know. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7329-->
<!--Post: 7330--><!--Time: 1108405325-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7330"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:witchkingofangmar@comcast.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Witchking<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Witchking<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 10:22 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I was going over the Zodiac&#39;s cyphers and his famous left over letters and wondered if BTK had used similar terminology. It&#39;s not easy or it would have been solved by now. I think somewhere in these cyphers a major clue resides that pieced with others tells the tale. <BR> <BR>I&#39;m close on this one I feel.....but then again I MAY be dropping a bombshell soon. Not to be boastful, but if a little &#39;fishing expedition&#39; is successful, we&#39;ll have a dearth of info soon...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7330-->
<!--Post: 7343--><!--Time: 1108411882-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7343"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ztargate<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ztargate<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 12:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->In the list of chapters, one of the chapters is called &#34;Kits&#34;. So, most people assume that kit stands for BTK&#39;s &#34;murder kit&#34;. But, if one searches an acronym dictionary, one of the definitions is: <BR> <BR>The Kilmann Insight Test &#40;KIT&#41; created 02/1975 <BR> <BR>! <BR> <BR>It&#39;s a &#34;tool&#34; created by the Thomas-Killman team, to test some &amp;&#40;&#42;#@# of values and personalities and blah blah blah. <BR> <BR>Notice how it was introduced in 1975... around the time of the murders.  <BR> <BR>Hmmm... <BR> <BR><a href="http://acronym.langenberg.com/" target=_top>http://acronym.langenberg.com/</a> search here, then the definition at the bottom. <BR> <BR>:|<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7343-->
<!--Post: 7345--><!--Time: 1108412618-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7345"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:witchkingofangmar@comcast.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Witchking<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Witchking<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 12:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->thanks ztargate... <BR> <BR>The link is appreciated<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7345-->
<!--Post: 7526--><!--Time: 1108559156-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7526"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 5:05 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If you get a chance go to the threads BTK&#39;s True Initials and the thread for puzzles, when I was a kid we use to do the puzzles in the games mags. The criptiquotes are what got me hooked on puzzles. Maybe we can deciper these codes together. The BTK is broken down to mean That It is a Tragedy that you still demand physical evidence that I am the one, and the 1864 1684 has a meaning in Kansas Year Wichita was formed and 1684 Is the NID# for the web site at WSU, S. OldManor is that we know it&#39;s him because he still sends us evidence and comminicates with us in the same old manor.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
